{"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Ensembles synchronizes SQLite stores by recording local changes as events and exchanging them through a cloud backend. It works with both Core Data and SwiftData.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Using SwiftData?"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" See ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SwiftDataIntegration","type":"reference"},{"text":" for a complete guide — you never need to touch Core Data directly.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This guide covers Core Data setup, starting with a complete working example using ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleContainer","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Develop-with-Claude-Code","level":2,"text":"Develop with Claude Code"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If you use ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/claude.com\/claude-code","type":"reference"},{"text":", install the Ensembles skill first. It teaches Claude the API, the cloud backends, Ensembles 2 → 3 migration, the seed policy, and the common pitfalls, so it writes correct setup code and diagnoses sync issues without hand-holding:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["\/plugin marketplace add mentalfaculty\/Ensembles3","\/plugin install ensembles@ensembles"],"syntax":null},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Add-Ensembles-to-Your-Project","level":2,"text":"Add Ensembles to Your Project"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add the Ensembles package to your ","type":"text"},{"code":"Package.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or via Xcode’s package dependencies:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["https:\/\/github.com\/mentalfaculty\/Ensembles3.git"],"syntax":null},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Import the core module and one cloud backend:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import Ensembles","import EnsemblesCloudKit   \/\/ or EnsemblesLocalFile, EnsemblesMemory"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Complete-Example-Core-Data-with-CloudKit","level":2,"text":"Complete Example: Core Data with CloudKit"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Here’s a complete, working setup for a SwiftUI app that syncs via CloudKit. This uses ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleContainer","type":"reference"},{"text":", which creates the Core Data stack for you and syncs automatically.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"1-Create-Your-Core-Data-Model","level":3,"text":"1. Create Your Core Data Model"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In Xcode, add a ","type":"text"},{"code":".xcdatamodeld","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" file to your project (e.g., ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Model.xcdatamodeld"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":"). Define your entities as usual. For this example, we’ll assume a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Note","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" entity with ","type":"text"},{"code":"title","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (String) and ","type":"text"},{"code":"uniqueID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (String) attributes.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"2-Define-Your-Model-with-Syncable","level":3,"text":"2. Define Your Model with `Syncable`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For deduplication, conform your ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSManagedObject","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" subclass to the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/Syncable","type":"reference"},{"text":" protocol and specify which property holds the global identifier. A UUID assigned at creation time is usually the best choice:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import CoreData","import Ensembles","","class Note: NSManagedObject, Syncable {","    static let globalIdentifierKey = \"uniqueID\"","    @NSManaged var uniqueID: String","    @NSManaged var title: String","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A global identifier "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"must never change","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" once it has been assigned. Changing it after sync has begun will cause duplicates or data loss."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","style":"important","name":"Important"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use a fixed, meaningful value instead of a UUID for singleton objects or reference data like tags, where two devices might independently create the same logical object.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"3-Set-Up-the-Container","level":3,"text":"3. Set Up the Container"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiftUI","import Ensembles","import EnsemblesCloudKit","","@main","struct MyApp: App {","    let syncContainer: CoreDataEnsembleContainer","","    init() {","        \/\/ The model URL points to the .momd bundle compiled from your .xcdatamodeld","        let modelURL = Bundle.main.url(forResource: \"Model\", withExtension: \"momd\")!","","        \/\/ This creates a full Core Data stack automatically:","        \/\/ - SQLite store at Application Support\/MyNotes.sqlite","        \/\/ - Main-queue viewContext for your UI","        \/\/ - Auto-sync on save, on app activation, and on a 5-minute timer","        let container = CoreDataEnsembleContainer(","            name: \"MyNotes\",","            modelURL: modelURL,","            cloudFileSystem: CloudKitFileSystem(","                privateDatabaseForUbiquityContainerIdentifier: \"iCloud.com.example.mynotes\",","                schemaVersion: .v2","            )","        )!","","        self.syncContainer = container","    }","","    var body: some Scene {","        WindowGroup {","            ContentView()","                .environment(","                    \\.managedObjectContext,","                    syncContainer.viewContext","                )","        }","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"That’s the complete setup. The container discovers ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/Syncable","type":"reference"},{"text":" conformances automatically, attaches to the cloud, and begins syncing. Remote changes are merged into ","type":"text"},{"code":"viewContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" so your UI stays up to date.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"text":"4. Respond to Events (Optional)","type":"heading","anchor":"4-Respond-to-Events-Optional"},{"code":["\/\/ Called after remote changes are merged into viewContext","container.didSaveMergeChanges = { notification in","    print(\"Merged remote changes\")","}","","\/\/ Called if a sync fails","container.didEncounterError = { error in","    print(\"Sync error: \\(error)\")","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Using-a-Custom-Store-Location","level":2,"text":"Using a Custom Store Location"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you need control over where the SQLite file lives, pass an explicit "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"storeURL"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let appSupport = FileManager.default.urls(","    for: .applicationSupportDirectory, in: .userDomainMask",").first!","let storeURL = appSupport.appendingPathComponent(\"MyApp\/data.sqlite\")","try FileManager.default.createDirectory(","    at: storeURL.deletingLastPathComponent(),","    withIntermediateDirectories: true",")","","let container = CoreDataEnsembleContainer(","    name: \"MyNotes\",","    storeURL: storeURL,","    modelURL: Bundle.main.url(forResource: \"Model\", withExtension: \"momd\")!,","    cloudFileSystem: CloudKitFileSystem(","        privateDatabaseForUbiquityContainerIdentifier: \"iCloud.com.example.mynotes\",","        schemaVersion: .v2","    )",")!"]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Working-with-an-Existing-Core-Data-Stack","text":"Working with an Existing Core Data Stack"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If you already have an ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSPersistentContainer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", pass it in directly:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let container = CoreDataEnsembleContainer(","    persistentContainer: myPersistentContainer,","    cloudFileSystem: cloudFS",")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Or if you have an existing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSManagedObjectContext"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let container = CoreDataEnsembleContainer(","    name: \"MyNotes\",","    viewContext: myContext,","    persistentStoreURL: myStoreURL,","    managedObjectModel: myContext.persistentStoreCoordinator!.managedObjectModel,","    managedObjectModels: nil,","    cloudFileSystem: cloudFS",")"]},{"type":"heading","text":"Auto-Sync Configuration","anchor":"Auto-Sync-Configuration","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Control when syncing occurs with "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/AutoSyncPolicy"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let config = EnsembleContainerConfiguration(","    autoSyncPolicy: [.onSave, .onTimer],   \/\/ Sync on save and timer, not on activation","    timerInterval: 30                       \/\/ Timer fires every 30 seconds",")","let container = CoreDataEnsembleContainer(","    name: \"MyNotes\",","    modelURL: modelURL,","    cloudFileSystem: cloudFS,","    configuration: config",")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Set "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"autoSyncPolicy"},{"type":"text","text":" to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".manual"},{"type":"text","text":" and call "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleContainer\/sync()"},{"type":"text","text":" yourself for full control over timing."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Backward Compatibility with Ensembles 2","anchor":"Backward-Compatibility-with-Ensembles-2","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If you’re transitioning from Ensembles 2 and some users may still be on E2, set the compatibility mode:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let config = EnsembleContainerConfiguration(","    compatibilityMode: .ensembles2Compatible",")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This restricts exports to formats that Ensembles 2 peers can parse. Switch to ","type":"text"},{"code":".ensembles3","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (the default) once all users have upgraded.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"The Manual Way: CoreDataEnsemble","anchor":"The-Manual-Way-CoreDataEnsemble","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For more control over the sync lifecycle, use ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble"},{"text":" directly. This is useful when you need to manage attach\/detach timing, handle specific delegate methods, or integrate with a complex Core Data stack.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Create and Attach","anchor":"Create-and-Attach","level":3},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import Ensembles","import EnsemblesCloudKit","","\/\/ Get the store URL from your persistent store coordinator","let store = persistentStoreCoordinator.persistentStores.first!","let storeURL = store.url!","let modelURL = Bundle.main.url(forResource: \"Model\", withExtension: \"momd\")!","","let ensemble = CoreDataEnsemble(","    ensembleIdentifier: \"MyNotes\",","    persistentStoreURL: storeURL,","    managedObjectModelURL: modelURL,","    cloudFileSystem: CloudKitFileSystem(","        privateDatabaseForUbiquityContainerIdentifier: \"iCloud.com.example.mynotes\",","        schemaVersion: .v2","    )",")","ensemble?.delegate = self","","\/\/ Attach registers this device in the cloud","try await ensemble?.attachPersistentStore()"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/ensembleIdentifier","type":"reference"},{"text":" must be the same on all devices that should sync together. If you have multiple persistent stores, create one ensemble per store with a unique identifier.","type":"text"}]},{"name":"Important","type":"aside","style":"important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Avoid saving to the persistent store while attaching. If a save is detected, attachment will fail with an error and you will need to retry."}]}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Sync Changes","anchor":"Sync-Changes"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Call "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/sync(options:)"},{"text":" periodically — for example, when the app enters the foreground, on a timer, or in response to a push notification:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["try await ensemble?.sync()"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A sync downloads remote events, replays them into the local store, and uploads new local events. Sync errors are usually transient — just retry later."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Handle the Delegate","anchor":"Handle-the-Delegate"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Implement "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleDelegate"},{"type":"text","text":" to respond to sync events. The most important method merges remote changes into your main context:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["extension AppDelegate: CoreDataEnsembleDelegate {","    func coreDataEnsemble(","        _ ensemble: CoreDataEnsemble,","        didSaveMergeChangesWith notification: Notification","    ) {","        viewContext.perform {","            self.viewContext.mergeChanges(fromContextDidSave: notification)","        }","    }","}"]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"With ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleContainer"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/Syncable"},{"text":" conformances are discovered automatically and no ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"globalIdentifiersForManagedObjects"},{"text":" implementation is needed. When you use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CoreDataEnsemble"},{"text":" directly, the delegate method is required — but if your classes conform to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Syncable"},{"text":" it is a one-liner:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["func coreDataEnsemble(","    _ ensemble: CoreDataEnsemble,","    globalIdentifiersForManagedObjects objects: [NSManagedObject]",") -> [String] {","    ensemble.syncableGlobalIdentifiers(forManagedObjects: objects)","}"],"syntax":"swift"}],"name":"Tip","type":"aside","style":"tip"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Other delegate methods let you:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Inspect and repair merge data","type":"text"}]},{"text":" before it’s committed (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"shouldSaveMergedChangesIn:reparationContext:"},{"text":")","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Handle save failures","type":"text"}]},{"text":" during merging (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"didFailToSaveMergedChangesIn:error:reparationContext:"},{"text":")","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"React to forced detaches","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" caused by identity changes or data corruption ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"didDetachWithError:"},{"type":"text","text":")"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"See "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/ConflictResolution","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for more on conflict handling and the reparation context.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Detach","anchor":"Detach"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To stop syncing, detach from the cloud:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["try await ensemble?.detachPersistentStore()"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This removes local sync data (event logs and metadata). The persistent store itself is not affected. You can re-attach later to resume syncing.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Seed Policies","anchor":"Seed-Policies"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SeedPolicy","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" parameter controls how existing data in the store is handled during attachment:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SeedPolicy\/mergeAllData"},{"type":"text","text":" (default) — Imports local data so it can be merged with data from other devices."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SeedPolicy\/excludeLocalData"},{"type":"text","text":" — Ignores local data. Use this when you want to start fresh from cloud data."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Sync Options","anchor":"Sync-Options"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For advanced control, pass ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SyncOptions","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ Download only — don't integrate or upload","try await ensemble?.sync(options: .cloudFileRetrievalOnly)","","\/\/ Force a rebase to compact sync history","try await ensemble?.sync(options: .forceRebase)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A rebase is the most expensive part of a sync, and Ensembles decides for itself when one is due. To choose the moment yourself, sync with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SyncOptions\/suppressRebase","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" in normal use, and when conditions suit (the device is charging, a background processing task is running) read ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/rebaseMetrics()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and pass ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SyncOptions\/forceRebase","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" if ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/RebaseMetrics\/isRebaseRecommended","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is true or your own thresholds are met.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Process Pending Changes","anchor":"Process-Pending-Changes"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"On iOS, the app may be suspended before Ensembles finishes recording a save. Call ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/processPendingChanges()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — for example, in a background task — to ensure all changes are fully stored:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["try await ensemble?.processPendingChanges()"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Monitor Activity","anchor":"Monitor-Activity"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Track long-running operations via ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/currentActivity","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/activityProgress","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", or observe these notifications:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreDataEnsembleDidBeginActivity"},{"type":"text","text":" — An activity started"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreDataEnsembleDidMakeProgressWithActivity"},{"type":"text","text":" — Progress updated (includes "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SyncingPhase"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/AttachingPhase"},{"type":"text","text":")"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"coreDataEnsembleWillEndActivity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — An activity finished (may include an error)","type":"text"}]}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ensembles\/gettingstarted"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Essentials","anchor":"Essentials","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SwiftDataIntegration","doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SyncLifecycle","doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleContainer","doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble","doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleDelegate"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"metadata":{"title":"Getting Started","roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Ensembles"}]},"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/GettingStarted"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Set up Ensembles to sync a Core Data or SwiftData persistent store across devices."}],"references":{"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/CoreDataEnsemble/currentActivity":{"title":"currentActivity","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/currentActivity","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The activity currently being undertaken, if any."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/coredataensemble\/currentactivity","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"currentActivity"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:9Ensembles16EnsembleActivityO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"EnsembleActivity"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/SyncingPhase":{"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SyncingPhase"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The phase of a sync operation currently in progress.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/syncingphase","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SyncingPhase","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SyncingPhase","kind":"symbol","title":"SyncingPhase"},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/ConflictResolution":{"title":"Conflict Resolution","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/ConflictResolution","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Understand how Ensembles resolves conflicts and how to customize the process."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/conflictresolution","type":"topic","kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/Syncable":{"title":"Syncable","abstract":[{"text":"A protocol for model types that declare how to derive a global identifier","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for Ensembles deduplication.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Syncable","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/syncable","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/Syncable","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Syncable","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/SyncOptions":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SyncOptions","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Options that control which phases of a sync are executed.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/syncoptions","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SyncOptions","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SyncOptions","kind":"symbol","title":"SyncOptions"},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/AutoSyncPolicy":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AutoSyncPolicy","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Controls when automatic merges occur.","type":"